    "confidence": 1.0,
    "explanation": "To the rider: part of your claim succeeds. To the driver: the distance allegation fails, but one fare line needs correcting.\n\nThe fare. This was an upfront-quoted trip (EV-FARE-00803: fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE, quoted_fare_sgd 18.00, total_charged 24.00). The itemised base fare 3.80 + distance fare 6.00 + time fare 7.40 + platform fee 0.80 sum exactly to the 18.00 quote, and the billed distance (distance_charged_km 2.93) equals the trace distance, so no distance or time line is overstated. The whole 6.00 difference is the airport_surcharge line. The trip started at Bugis Victoria Street and ended at Suntec City Temasek Boulevard (EV-TRIP-00803), so it did not originate at Changi or Seletar and no airport surcharge is chargeable. Under POL-RD-09(4) this is a billing-integrity failure and the SGD 6.00 is refunded in full as a standalone correction; POL-RD-11(a) reaches the same figure (SGD 24.00 charged minus SGD 18.00 quoted minus SGD 0.00 of properly chargeable pass-throughs = SGD 6.00). These are the same SGD 6.00, not two payments, and are not added together (POL-RD-11(b)). Nothing offsets it: the derived erp_lines and erp total are SGD 0.00, the waiting_time_fee is SGD 0.00, and the airport surcharge is the only non-zero statutory line (EV-FARE-00803). Your request for the entire SGD 24.00 is refused: on an upfront-quoted fare the distance and time charges were fixed at booking and those lines were properly incurred.\n\nThe distance. The governing trace (EV-GPS-00803) measures 2.93 km against a booked optimal of 2.20 km, an excess of 0.73 km — 33.18% of optimal, which passes the percentage limb of POL-RD-01 but fails the 0.8 km absolute limb. No deviation is therefore established, and on an upfront-quoted fare POL-RD-02 would not run in any event (POL-RD-11). On this point the driver's reading is correct: both establishment limbs must pass, and the artifact's own derived status reads 'no deviation'. Both advocates are answered together on this.\n\nNo exculpatory clause displaces either conclusion. The chat log for this trip is empty (EV-CHAT-00803: message_count 0), so no rider-requested detour under POL-RD-04 can be asserted or corroborated; pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are both null, so POL-RD-05 does not apply and no substitute figure may be derived; vehicle_type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so the pooled baseline of POL-RD-12 is not in play. The booked optimal therefore stands at 2.20 km.\n\nThe traffic advisory. EV-ADVIS-00803-01 is MISSING, admissibility status MISSING with issue MISSING_ARTIFACT and weight_multiplier 0.0. Because no advisory record covers this trip, POL-RD-03 cannot be run and no external traffic cause carries weight (POL-RD-13). This does not escalate: the missing advisory was not invoked as an exculpatory clause against itself — the driver cites its absence only to fix the baseline — so POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged. A separate rider claim about the advisory was discarded by the referee for citing the impaired artifact without naming its issue code, and is not reinstated here.\n\nThe trace is unimpaired: 52 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, an empty gaps list and a maximum inter-fix gap of 10 seconds, so none of POL-RD-07(a) to (c) is met and neither POL-RD-07 nor POL-RD-10(3) is in play. Trip identifiers (TRP-00803) match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown, and no POL-RD-10 trigger fires.\n\nRepeat-deviation check: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 over completed_trips_90d of 300, so no pattern is established and no POL-RD-06 FULL_REFUND uplift or conduct referral arises. The uncited traffic assertions and the lifetime counters on the profiles are given no weight (POL-GEN-01, POL-RD-08); the mention of prior_deviation_flags is context only and was flagged, not relied on.\n\nConfidence. The deciding facts — the amount charged over the quote (EV-FARE-00803) and the trip's non-airport origin (EV-TRIP-00803) — are carried by artifacts at weight_multiplier 1.0, so confidence is 1.0. The monetary effect of SGD 6.00 does not exceed the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold (POL-GEN-05), so this ruling executes on issue; execution releases the fare correction under POL-GEN-04's appeal route.\n\nOutcome: PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 6.00 to the rider, with the billing-integrity referral above; no driver compensation is payable (the billed distance equals the trace distance, so there is no unbilled-distance shortfall under POL-RD-04)."
  },
