    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) — billing integrity: an airport surcharge of SGD 6.00 was charged on trip TRP-00803, which originated at Bugis Victoria Street and ended at Suntec City Temasek Boulevard, not at Changi or Seletar Airport. The line is not properly chargeable and is refunded in full."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider, and to the driver.\n\nTHE ROUTE POINT. The governing GPS trace (EV-GPS-00803) measures 2.93 km between the boarded and alighted events, against a booked optimal of 2.20 km on the trip record (EV-TRIP-00803): an excess of 0.73 km, or 33.18% of optimal. POL-RD-01 requires BOTH an excess above 20% of optimal AND an excess above 0.8 km. The percentage limb passes; the absolute limb fails, because 0.73 km is below 0.8 km. No route deviation is established on this trip, so the rider's 'the journey was longer than needed' ground carries no weight. Independently, this fare is UPFRONT_QUOTE (fare_model on EV-FARE-00803), so under POL-RD-11 the distance and time charges were fixed at booking and no distance-or-time refund is available however large the excess. The trace is clean (52 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps), so POL-RD-07 gap handling is not in play and no POL-RD-10 trigger fires. The driver's no-deviation argument is accepted on both grounds.\n\nTHE MONEY. The non-surcharge lines — base fare 3.80 + distance fare 6.00 + time fare 7.40 + platform fee 0.80 — sum to exactly the SGD 18.00 quoted at booking, and the billed distance (distance_charged_km 2.93 km) equals the trace distance, so no distance or time line is overstated. The whole of the SGD 6.00 difference is the itemised airport_surcharge line. An airport surcharge is chargeable only on a trip ORIGINATING at Changi or Seletar Airport. This trip began at Bugis Victoria Street and ended at Suntec City Temasek Boulevard, so the surcharge was not chargeable at all: under POL-RD-09(4) it is a billing-integrity failure, refunded in full as a standalone correction, available whether or not a deviation exists. POL-RD-11(a) produces the same figure from the other direction: charged_total 24.00 less quoted_fare 18.00 less properly chargeable pass-throughs 0.00 (no ERP lines, waiting_time_fee 0.00, the surcharge not chargeable) = SGD 6.00, rounded up to SGD 6.00. These are the same money reached two ways and are NOT added together. The rider's request for the entire SGD 24.00 is refused: SGD 18.00 of it is the properly quoted fare the rider agreed to. The driver's claim that the SGD 6.00 is a pass-through item that settles separately is accepted as to how it is settled, but not as to chargeability — the pass-through is only chargeable where the trip originates at an airport, which this one did not.\n\nNO OTHER ADJUSTMENT. POL-RD-03 cannot run (no traffic advisory covers this trip), POL-RD-04 cannot run (the chat log EV-CHAT-00803 has no messages, so no rider-requested detour is even asserted), POL-RD-05 does not apply (no amendment timestamps; amended_optimal_distance_km is null), and POL-RD-12 does not apply (vehicle_type RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL). No repeat-deviation pattern exists against the driver — deviation_flags_90d 0 against completed_trips_90d 300 — so no POL-RD-06 uplift or conduct referral arises; the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is context only and was not used.\n\nCONFIDENCE AND EXECUTION. The deciding fact — the over-quote of SGD 6.00 — is carried by EV-FARE-00803 at weight 1.0 and by EV-TRIP-00803 at weight 1.0, so confidence is capped at 1.0 and is set at 0.95. The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00803-01 (weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT) is relied on only as a citable absence; no part of this ruling is carried by it. The rider's separate claim that named that artifact without disclosing its issue code was discarded at the mechanical citation check and is recorded in the audit. The monetary effect, SGD 6.00, does not exceed the SGD 8.00 execution threshold in POL-GEN-05, so this provisional ruling executes automatically on issue, subject to the appeal route under POL-GEN-04."
  },
