    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: this dispute is about SGD 24.00 charged against an upfront booking quote of SGD 18.00 (EV-FARE-00803). The fare was booked as an UPFRONT_QUOTE, so under POL-RD-11 the distance and time charges were locked at booking and no distance-or-time refund is available to the rider however the trip is characterised; POL-RD-02 does not run on this fare model. The non-surcharge itemisation (base fare 3.80 + distance fare 6.00 + time fare 7.40 + platform fee 0.80 = 18.00) matches the quote exactly, and the billed distance (2.93 km) equals the trace distance, so no distance or time line is overstated.\n\nNo route deviation is established, and both sides agree on this. The governing trace figure is 2.93 km (EV-GPS-00803) against the booked optimal of 2.2 km (EV-TRIP-00803), an excess of 0.73 km, which is 33.18% of optimal. POL-RD-01 requires BOTH an excess above 20% and an excess above 0.8 km in absolute terms; the 0.73 km excess fails the absolute limb, so no deviation exists and the artifact's own 'no deviation' status stands. I accept the driver's claims on this point and the rider's corresponding concession. The gps_trace is clean and unimpaired for policy purposes (52 fixes, 10-second interval against an expected 10 seconds, 100% coverage, empty gaps list, no inter-fix jump above 500 m), so POL-RD-07 is not engaged and no POL-RD-10 escalation arises on that ground. Trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown (TRP-00803), timestamps run forwards and agree, and the missing traffic advisory has no bearing because no party asserts an external traffic cause.\n\nThe money turns on the one line that does not belong to the SGD 18.00 quote: the itemised airport surcharge of SGD 6.00. Trip TRP-00803 originates at Bugis Victoria Street and ends at Suntec City Temasek Boulevard, so it does not originate at Changi or Seletar Airport. Under POL-RD-09(4) an airport surcharge on a trip that does not originate at an airport is a billing-integrity failure; it is refunded in full as a standalone correction, and it is available whether or not a deviation exists. The properly chargeable pass-through total is SGD 0.00 (no ERP gantries crossed, waiting-time fee 0.00). Running POL-RD-11(a): charged_total 24.00 less quoted_fare_sgd 18.00 less properly chargeable pass-throughs 0.00 = SGD 6.00 refundable in full. I do not add POL-RD-09(4)'s SGD 6.00 on top of that figure; they are the same SGD 6.00 and counting it twice would refund it twice.\n\nOn the rider's claims: the request for the entire SGD 24.00 is rejected, because the distance and time lines are closed by the upfront quote and the fare record shows no overcharge on them; the entitlement is SGD 6.00, as the rider's own advocate accepted. On the driver's claims: the SGD 6.00 is indeed the airport surcharge and not a distance or time overcharge, but that does not resist the refund — an airport surcharge wrongly applied is refunded under POL-RD-09(4). No exculpatory clause applies to reduce the excess: the chat log for this trip is empty (POL-RD-04 unavailable), no pickup or dropoff amendment timestamp exists and amended_optimal_distance_km is null (POL-RD-05 unavailable), and the vehicle type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL (POL-RD-12 inapplicable). No repeat-deviation pattern exists under POL-RD-06 (deviation_flags_90d 0 against completed_trips_90d 300, a ratio of 0.00 against a trigger of 0.05), so no FULL_REFUND uplift and no conduct referral arise. The lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags mentioned in the driver's claim is context only under POL-GEN-01 and was not used as a ground.\n\nOn confidence: the deciding facts — the charged total, the quote, and the absence of an airport origin — are carried by EV-FARE-00803 and EV-TRIP-00803, both at weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0. The MISSING traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00803-01, weight 0.0) carries no deciding fact and does not drag the cap. Confidence is 0.95, above the 0.70 floor. The refund of SGD 6.00 does not exceed the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so it executes automatically, subject to the appeal route under POL-GEN-04. The billing-integrity finding is recorded as a referral under POL-RD-09(4) and does not displace or delay the money."
