{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 6.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity review: EV-FARE-00803 itemises an airport surcharge of SGD 6.00 on trip TRP-00803, which ran Bugis Victoria Street to Suntec City Temasek Boulevard and did not originate at Changi or Seletar Airport; the line is refunded in full as a standalone correction and the fare build should be reviewed."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver. The three core records carry the same trip identifier TRP-00803 and consistent timestamps, so the dispute is decided on the merits.\n\n1. NO ROUTE DEVIATION IS ESTABLISHED. Measured as POL-RD-01 requires, the governing gps_trace polyline is 2.93 km (EV-GPS-00803) against the booked optimal of 2.20 km (EV-TRIP-00803): an excess of 0.73 km. The percentage limb passes (0.73 km is 33.18% of 2.20 km, above the 20% gate) but the absolute limb fails (0.73 km is below the 0.8 km gate), and POL-RD-01 requires both. EV-ADVIS-00803-01 is MISSING (status MISSING, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight_multiplier 0.0), so no route adjustment under POL-RD-03 arises; no pickup or dropoff amendment is recorded, so POL-RD-05 does not arise; vehicle_type RYDE_X means POL-RD-12 does not arise; and the chat log is empty, so POL-RD-04 has nothing to corroborate. Both advocates reach this result and I accept it. The rider's 'the journey was longer than needed' ground is not made out, and it would in any event yield nothing on this fare.\n\n2. THE FARE WAS FIXED AT BOOKING. fare_breakdown.fare_model is UPFRONT_QUOTE with quoted_fare_sgd SGD 18.00. Under POL-RD-11 the distance and time charges were locked at booking and POL-RD-02 does not run, so no distance-or-time refund is available however long the drive. The rider's request that the entire SGD 24.00 be returned is refused on that ground, and the rider advocate rightly did not press it.\n\n3. WHAT IS REFUNDABLE IS THE OVER-QUOTE. Under POL-RD-11(a): charged_total SGD 24.00 less quoted_fare SGD 18.00 less the pass-through and statutory lines properly chargeable under POL-RD-09 (ERP SGD 0.00, waiting time fee SGD 0.00, airport surcharge SGD 0.00) = SGD 6.00, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05, so SGD 6.00. The whole of the difference is the itemised airport_surcharge of SGD 6.00, and this trip neither originated at Changi or Seletar nor ended at an airport, so under POL-RD-09(4) it is a billing-integrity failure refunded in full. That SGD 6.00 is the same sum as the POL-RD-11(a) figure, counted once and not twice. The base fare (3.80), distance fare (6.00), time fare (7.40) and platform fee (0.80) sum exactly to the SGD 18.00 quote, and the billed distance (2.93 km) equals the trace distance (2.93 km), so no other line is overstated. Outcome for the rider: PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 6.00 against a contested amount of SGD 24.00.\n\n4. DRIVER COMPENSATION: NONE. The billed distance equals the trace distance, so there is no unbilled-kilometre shortfall under POL-RD-04 and nothing is owed to the driver. The driver's POL-RD-06 point is accepted: deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 300, so no repeat-deviation pattern is established, no FULL_REFUND uplift applies and no driver-conduct referral arises. The lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is context only under POL-GEN-01 and has not been used.\n\n5. THE MISSING TRAFFIC ADVISORY. EV-ADVIS-00803-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0. Neither party asserts an external traffic cause as the explanation for a deviation, so POL-RD-03 has no assertion to test, the booked optimal route stands at 2.20 km, and POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged. The absence is disclosed and decides nothing. The rider's claim about that artifact was discarded at the mechanical stage for citing an impaired artifact without naming its issue code.\n\nCONFIDENCE. The deciding facts — the upfront quote, the charged total and the surcharge line — are carried by EV-FARE-00803 (weight 1.0) and EV-TRIP-00803 (weight 1.0), so the cap under POL-GEN-02(2) is 1.0 and my confidence is 0.95, above the 0.70 floor.\n\nREFERRAL. The POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity referral is recorded above. It rides with the money and does not delay it.\n\nEXECUTION AND APPEAL. The monetary effect is SGD 6.00, which does not exceed the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so under POL-GEN-05 the refund executes automatically. This is a provisional ruling made without human review; either party may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
  },
